WEBVTT

00:00.373 --> 00:03.752
♪ It seems today that all you see ♪

00:03.753 --> 00:07.056
♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪

00:07.057 --> 00:10.626
♪ But where are those good
old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.627 --> 00:13.629
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.630 --> 00:17.132
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.133 --> 00:20.469
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.470 --> 00:22.037
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.038 --> 00:23.672
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.673 --> 00:28.994
♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:38.664 --> 00:41.240
Hey, guys, I didn't know you were
coming to the church raffle.

00:41.241 --> 00:43.142
I will confess a mix-up to you.

00:43.143 --> 00:46.347
I thought Donna said we were
going to the "church waffle."

00:46.348 --> 00:49.047
And we're only here for the
fantasy weekend at Fenway Park.

00:49.048 --> 00:50.136
Fenway Park?

00:50.138 --> 00:52.127
Oh, yeah, the winner and
a friend get to hang out

00:52.129 --> 00:54.687
and practice with
retired Red Sox players

00:54.688 --> 00:58.524
and then play in a real game,
right on the field at Fenway.

00:58.525 --> 01:01.060
Oh, my God, that's always
been a dream of mine!

01:01.061 --> 01:03.939
Well, that and tuning a guitar
in front of a live audience.

01:26.421 --> 01:29.047
This was in perfect tune
when they handed it to me.

01:32.350 --> 01:36.236
Next up, our fantasy weekend
for two at Fenway Park.

01:36.238 --> 01:37.553
Oh, man, this is it!

01:37.555 --> 01:39.432
And the winner is...

01:39.433 --> 01:41.033
Peter Griffin!

01:41.034 --> 01:42.668
Holy crap, I won!

01:42.669 --> 01:44.470
- Wow, good for you!
- Congratulations!

01:44.471 --> 01:47.239
I like it when people
say your name out loud!

01:47.240 --> 01:48.808
How exciting, Peter.

01:48.809 --> 01:50.409
A weekend trip to Boston.

01:50.410 --> 01:51.644
Yeah, and the best part is,

01:51.645 --> 01:53.512
I don't even have to get on a plane.

01:53.513 --> 01:55.141
I always have trouble at the airport.

01:58.002 --> 01:59.852
Sir, you're not allowed
to be on the carousel.

01:59.853 --> 02:02.337
Well, then maybe you shouldn't
have named it such a fun word.

02:03.356 --> 02:05.248
Uh, excuse me, excuse me, I'm not yours.

02:05.250 --> 02:07.293
He's stealing me! I'm being stolen!

02:07.294 --> 02:09.171
Excuse me, I think you've got mine.

02:10.594 --> 02:11.954
Oh, that's a good idea.

02:19.623 --> 02:21.874
- Oh, hey, Quagmire.
- Hey, Peter.

02:21.875 --> 02:23.976
So I was just baking a coffee cake,

02:23.977 --> 02:25.511
and I figured I'd bring it over,

02:25.512 --> 02:26.979
'cause you like coffee cake.

02:26.980 --> 02:27.980
Wow, thanks.

02:27.981 --> 02:29.114
Yeah, yeah, no problem.

02:29.115 --> 02:30.899
- So, who are you taking to Fenway?
- What?

02:30.901 --> 02:33.026
Well, I was just thinking,
you have that extra ticket,

02:33.028 --> 02:35.402
- maybe you'd want to...
- Peter, before you answer him,

02:35.404 --> 02:39.191
I've got that murdered jogger's
Discman you wanted last week.

02:39.192 --> 02:40.593
Still bloody.

02:40.594 --> 02:43.796
Hi, Peter. You know how
you like $40 cash?

02:43.797 --> 02:46.464
Well, here's almost $40 cash.

02:46.465 --> 02:48.107
Guys, look, I know you all want to go,

02:48.108 --> 02:50.367
but I-I need a little more
time to figure this out.

02:50.368 --> 02:52.104
I mean, it's a tough decision.

02:52.105 --> 02:54.940
Like what to do with that
big watermelon I bought.

02:54.941 --> 02:57.144
Griffin, I just wanted to tell you...

02:58.229 --> 02:59.712
that's a great outfit.

02:59.713 --> 03:00.913
Keep it up.

03:00.914 --> 03:01.914
I knew it.

03:01.915 --> 03:04.142
I have to start trusting myself more.

03:05.603 --> 03:07.019
Man, I don't envy you.

03:07.020 --> 03:08.654
Whichever one of them
you bring to Fenway,

03:08.655 --> 03:10.289
the other two will be mad at you.

03:10.290 --> 03:11.590
I don't want to bring any of them.

03:11.591 --> 03:13.592
Those guys are all way
better than me at baseball.

03:13.593 --> 03:15.928
They'd just show me up
and ruin it for me.

03:15.929 --> 03:17.062
Why don't you bring Lois?

03:17.063 --> 03:18.330
She doesn't care about baseball,

03:18.331 --> 03:20.232
and that way nobody gets
their feelings hurt.

03:20.233 --> 03:21.750
Brian, that's a great idea.

03:21.752 --> 03:22.752
Thanks.

03:22.754 --> 03:27.705
- Is it new-tennis-ball great?
- It's three-new-tennis-balls great.

03:27.707 --> 03:28.707
I'm gonna get 'em all,
I'm gonna get 'em all,

03:28.708 --> 03:29.708
I'm gonna get 'em all!

03:36.819 --> 03:38.584
Mom, you're really going to Boston?

03:38.585 --> 03:40.319
I didn't even think you liked baseball.

03:40.320 --> 03:42.121
Oh, I'm not going for baseball,

03:42.122 --> 03:44.723
I-I'm going for shopping, the hotel spa,

03:44.724 --> 03:46.325
and two days of being away

03:46.326 --> 03:48.340
from you life-sucking turds.

03:48.342 --> 03:49.995
Anyway, be good.

03:49.996 --> 03:52.131
And while we're gone, Brian's in charge.

03:52.132 --> 03:53.148
Where is Brian?

03:54.251 --> 03:56.802
What's up, bitches?

03:56.803 --> 03:58.203
Oh, come on, Mom, really?

03:58.204 --> 03:59.605
I'm in high school,

03:59.606 --> 04:01.907
and you're still putting
the dog in charge?

04:01.908 --> 04:03.576
Believe me, Meg, you want me in charge.

04:03.577 --> 04:05.210
Stewie can be a bit of a handful.

04:05.211 --> 04:06.078
He's right, you know.

04:06.079 --> 04:08.714
I'm a total Taurus,
stubborn as they come.

04:08.715 --> 04:10.049
All right, fine, Meg.

04:10.050 --> 04:12.284
While we're away, you can be in charge.

04:12.285 --> 04:14.553
Come on, Lois, time to get to Fenway.

04:14.554 --> 04:16.822
Wow, Dad, you look awesome.

04:16.823 --> 04:19.633
But I thought you were gonna
dress like a baseball player.

04:19.634 --> 04:20.626
I am, Chris.

04:20.627 --> 04:23.429
I'm the type of player who arrives
at the stadium in a suit.

04:23.430 --> 04:25.331
With a tie knot as big as an apple.

04:25.332 --> 04:27.766
That's how you know I got mon-ay.

04:27.767 --> 04:30.252
All right, we'll see you guys Sunday.

04:31.655 --> 04:34.039
Okay, now you heard Mom
say I'm in charge,

04:34.040 --> 04:36.066
so I just want to lay
a few ground rules.

04:36.067 --> 04:36.678
Yeah.

04:36.680 --> 04:38.043
I promise we're gonna have fun,

04:38.044 --> 04:40.069
- but there will be a schedule just...
- Uh-huh.

04:40.071 --> 04:41.837
- To keep everything running smoothly.
- Sure, got to have boundaries.

04:41.839 --> 04:43.482
- And I may assign a chore or two...
- That's great, Meg.

04:43.483 --> 04:45.618
- Because it's actually more fun...
- Sounds like you got it all worked out.

04:45.619 --> 04:47.319
- When everyone pitches in.
- Hey, by the way...

04:47.320 --> 04:48.887
Ah!

04:48.888 --> 04:51.082
I'm gonna flush your
retainer down the toilet.

05:08.726 --> 05:11.677
Look at this, Lois, the
Fenway Park locker room.

05:11.678 --> 05:12.945
All right, Peter, I'm gonna go.

05:12.946 --> 05:15.381
You want to hand me some cash
in front of the other men

05:15.382 --> 05:16.882
so you feel powerful?

05:16.883 --> 05:20.002
Instead, why don't you just
take my Minions Discover Card?

05:21.238 --> 05:22.354
Hey, there, sluggers.

05:22.355 --> 05:24.690
Welcome to Red Sox Fantasy Weekend.

05:24.691 --> 05:26.225
Well, who's this?

05:26.226 --> 05:28.293
We've never had a lady
come out for this before.

05:28.294 --> 05:30.562
Oh, no, no, that's my wife,
she's just dropping me off.

05:30.563 --> 05:33.365
Yeah, you're nice, but I'm not staying.

05:33.366 --> 05:35.467
I don't know the first
thing about baseball.

05:35.468 --> 05:37.403
Look, your spot's already paid for.

05:37.404 --> 05:40.472
And besides, if you leave,
the teams will be lopsided.

05:40.473 --> 05:43.275
So, as your coach, I insist
you stay and play with us.

05:43.276 --> 05:44.643
Right, fellas?

05:46.079 --> 05:47.913
Well, I don't know.

05:47.914 --> 05:49.615
What do you think, Peter?

05:49.616 --> 05:51.950
What do I think about sharing
fantasy baseball camp

05:51.951 --> 05:53.052
with my wife?

05:53.053 --> 05:55.654
Yeah, come on, let her play.

05:55.655 --> 05:59.024
Wow, 1980s All-Star Wade Boggs!

05:59.025 --> 06:01.393
Hey, would you mind standing
next to a star of today?

06:01.394 --> 06:02.411
Sure.

06:03.514 --> 06:05.531
Man, what happened to our game?

06:05.532 --> 06:07.900
David Ortiz, will you
pick him up like a baby?

06:07.907 --> 06:09.407
It's your weekend.

06:10.770 --> 06:12.838
Now let me put this
baby bonnet on his head

06:12.839 --> 06:14.156
and a cigar in his mouth.

06:15.659 --> 06:16.942
So, what do you say?

06:16.943 --> 06:18.377
Are you gonna let your wife play?

06:18.378 --> 06:19.545
Absolutely.

06:19.546 --> 06:21.013
Lois, stay here and play with us.

06:21.014 --> 06:23.348
I can't say no to Baby Boggs.

06:23.349 --> 06:25.660
Coochie-coochie-coo... Ah, he bit me.

06:33.852 --> 06:35.969
Oh, my God, I can't believe I'm here.

06:35.970 --> 06:37.671
Lois, see that wall there?

06:37.672 --> 06:39.939
They call that "the Green Monster."

06:39.940 --> 06:43.476
And over there's where I threw a
D-cell battery at Jos├й Canseco.

06:43.477 --> 06:45.028
All right, let's play ball.

06:46.331 --> 06:48.481
Wow, you must be excited, Peter.

06:48.482 --> 06:51.351
Yep, guess I can cross this
one off my bucket list.

06:51.352 --> 06:54.771
All that's left now is
living the pueblo lifestyle.

06:56.274 --> 06:58.657
Peter, what the hell did
you do to the house?

06:58.659 --> 07:02.529
I know, it seems pretty lame
until you realize I'm 58.

07:02.530 --> 07:04.998
Now, if you'll excuse me, I
have to go lick the foot

07:04.999 --> 07:08.511
<i>of a fleshy, pale woman for Real Sex 34.</i>

07:13.931 --> 07:16.409
Rupert, what do you think of
this fan fiction I wrote?

07:16.410 --> 07:18.978
"Diego pressed Dora against the wall,

07:18.979 --> 07:20.413
her bosom heaving,

07:20.414 --> 07:23.049
her hot Latina breath on his face.

07:23.050 --> 07:26.753
For once, Diego was going
to do the exploring."

07:26.754 --> 07:28.788
Whew, just reading it...

07:28.789 --> 07:30.223
<i>muy caliente.</i>

07:30.224 --> 07:32.459
Okay, Stewie, time for
you to get dressed.

07:32.460 --> 07:34.811
Yeah, a closed door means
"come in," I guess.

07:35.859 --> 07:37.664
What the hell do you think you're doing?

07:37.665 --> 07:39.632
Let's pick out a cute shirt for you.

07:39.633 --> 07:41.501
Then I thought we can go to the park.

07:41.502 --> 07:42.635
Or, how about this?

07:42.636 --> 07:44.821
I press my butt against
the wall and dook on it?

07:45.857 --> 07:47.006
Stewie!

07:47.007 --> 07:48.041
Don't do that!

07:48.042 --> 07:49.209
You're messing with my schedule,

07:49.210 --> 07:51.010
so I'm giving you wall poo.

07:51.011 --> 07:52.579
Stop that right now.

07:52.580 --> 07:54.247
You just earned a time-out.

07:54.248 --> 07:55.749
A what? Let go of me!

07:55.750 --> 07:56.983
Don't you walk away!

07:56.984 --> 07:59.452
Hey, don't bruise me, I'm
going dancing later.

07:59.453 --> 08:01.521
You listen to me, you little monster,

08:01.522 --> 08:03.723
I take abuse from everybody around here,

08:03.724 --> 08:05.959
but I am not gonna take it from you.

08:05.960 --> 08:08.194
Now sit here until I say you can get up.

08:08.195 --> 08:10.397
And if you move one muscle before then,

08:10.398 --> 08:12.599
I'll smack you in your weird head.

08:12.600 --> 08:14.167
Hey, it's not weird.

08:14.168 --> 08:16.454
Mom says it's distinctive.

08:25.530 --> 08:26.829
Griffin, you're up.

08:30.268 --> 08:32.185
It's always the fat one.

08:32.186 --> 08:33.086
I heard that.

08:33.087 --> 08:34.854
I said it right to you.

08:34.855 --> 08:35.716
You know what?

08:35.718 --> 08:37.290
Let's just get Lois up to bat.

08:37.291 --> 08:38.425
Where's Lois?

08:38.426 --> 08:40.393
I'm right here, Coach.

08:40.394 --> 08:42.829
Guess you don't have a
lot of babes out here.

08:42.830 --> 08:45.131
Except for Babe Ruth.

08:47.101 --> 08:48.234
- Babe Ruth.
- Ha!

08:48.235 --> 08:49.952
That's funny 'cause she's hot.

08:53.808 --> 08:55.708
Ah, it's a little like tennis.

08:55.709 --> 08:57.510
Uh, did you see that, Peter?

08:57.511 --> 08:58.878
I'm doing it all!

08:58.879 --> 09:01.230
Damn it. This is supposed
to be my weekend.

09:12.544 --> 09:13.526
Stewie?

09:13.527 --> 09:14.661
What the hell's going on?

09:14.662 --> 09:15.929
Meg's awful!

09:15.930 --> 09:18.631
She gave me a time-out and she
made me sit in this chair.

09:18.632 --> 09:21.034
My God, she put eye shadow on you, too.

09:21.035 --> 09:23.269
I might've gotten up from the chair.

09:23.270 --> 09:24.771
Brian, Meg's lost her mind.

09:24.772 --> 09:26.005
You've got to talk to her.

09:26.006 --> 09:27.674
Stewie, Lois put Meg in charge,

09:27.675 --> 09:29.976
and, honestly, once I knew that,

09:29.977 --> 09:31.177
I ate a pot cookie.

09:31.178 --> 09:33.012
So, um, yeah.

09:33.013 --> 09:34.447
So good luck with all that.

09:34.448 --> 09:36.783
Uh, you got any cool DVDs?

09:36.784 --> 09:38.151
Brian, please, I need help.

09:38.152 --> 09:39.185
Totally.

09:39.186 --> 09:40.386
Hey, where's Chris?

09:40.387 --> 09:42.689
I wonder if he'll play
Wii bowling with me.

09:42.690 --> 09:44.858
All right, that's it, I'm
not just gonna sit here

09:44.859 --> 09:46.392
and see what that psycho does next.

09:46.393 --> 09:47.393
All right, think.

09:47.394 --> 09:48.495
Ah!

09:48.496 --> 09:50.396
I shall fashion a makeshift ladder

09:50.397 --> 09:53.199
with my Diaper Genie entrails,
shimmy down to the yard,

09:53.200 --> 09:54.968
and I'm free.

09:54.969 --> 09:56.903
The trick, Chris, is
thinking of the wand

09:56.904 --> 09:59.239
as an extension of your arm.

09:59.240 --> 10:01.374
Wow, I can't believe I'm pretend bowling

10:01.375 --> 10:02.859
with a dog on drugs!

10:06.297 --> 10:07.797
Ah! Son of a bitch!

10:11.185 --> 10:12.552
Oh, my God, a baby!

10:12.553 --> 10:13.820
My name's Shelly.

10:13.821 --> 10:15.255
I can't have any of my own.

10:15.256 --> 10:17.123
Would you like to come home with me?

10:17.124 --> 10:18.324
I love you so much.

10:18.325 --> 10:20.176
Ah! Everywhere's a nightmare!

10:32.323 --> 10:35.341
Wow, it's nice they put
on a banquet for you.

10:35.342 --> 10:37.443
It looks like I'm the only woman here.

10:37.444 --> 10:38.645
Yeah, they're ex-athletes,

10:38.646 --> 10:40.113
which means they're all divorced.

10:40.114 --> 10:42.115
In fact, their ex-wives are
having a banquet next door

10:42.116 --> 10:43.383
with their money.

10:45.986 --> 10:47.854
Oh, they're having fun.

10:47.855 --> 10:49.989
They're doing a lot of pointing dancing.

10:53.160 --> 10:55.295
Well, at least somebody's
having fun here tonight.

10:55.296 --> 10:58.064
Oh, you're just nervous about
the big game tomorrow.

10:58.065 --> 11:00.533
I-Is it 'cause of how pink
you turn when you run?

11:00.534 --> 11:03.002
A couple guys mentioned
that today on the field.

11:03.003 --> 11:04.203
What? Who said that?

11:04.204 --> 11:06.072
I don't know, "N-Nomar" something.

11:06.073 --> 11:07.407
You met Nomar?!

11:07.408 --> 11:08.808
Hey, there you are.

11:08.809 --> 11:10.977
We've been saving a spot
at the head table for you

11:10.978 --> 11:12.045
with all the Hall-of-Famers.

11:12.046 --> 11:13.379
Oh, thanks.

11:13.380 --> 11:15.181
Finally something's going my way.

11:15.182 --> 11:17.951
- Where should I...
- Not you. Lois.

11:17.952 --> 11:19.118
What?

11:21.622 --> 11:23.723
This is the one night of the year

11:23.724 --> 11:26.192
they let me out of the scoreboard.

11:26.193 --> 11:29.295
Oh, I don't know if I deserve
to sit at the head table.

11:29.296 --> 11:30.897
No, no, we took a vote.

11:30.898 --> 11:32.465
We all want to sit next to you.

11:32.466 --> 11:33.866
You're the only one
here who doesn't have

11:33.867 --> 11:36.302
a fistful of baseball
cards for us to sign.

11:36.303 --> 11:37.737
I wasn't gonna have 'em sign 'em.

11:37.738 --> 11:39.505
I was just gonna tell 'em their stats.

11:39.506 --> 11:41.374
But this is Peter's weekend.

11:41.375 --> 11:42.976
Aw, don't worry about Peter.

11:42.977 --> 11:45.044
Now, come on, Lois,
we've got you sitting

11:45.045 --> 11:46.913
right between Pedro Martinez

11:46.914 --> 11:49.248
and Ted Williams' severed head.

11:49.249 --> 11:51.017
There's a special place in hell

11:51.018 --> 11:54.203
for whoever's responsible
for me ending up like this.

11:59.644 --> 12:02.395
Hey, Meg, is anybody gonna
eat this grilled cheese?

12:02.396 --> 12:04.897
No, don't eat that.
That's Stewie's lunch.

12:04.898 --> 12:06.733
Oh, my God, Stewie!

12:06.734 --> 12:09.485
I forgot, he's been in a
time-out for six hours.

12:11.589 --> 12:14.474
Stewie? Oh, no, where is he?

12:14.475 --> 12:17.310
He's gone... I'm gonna
be in so much trouble.

12:17.311 --> 12:19.445
I tried to tell you,
watching Stewie wasn't easy.

12:19.446 --> 12:22.582
Oh... Aw, man, this is terrible.

12:22.583 --> 12:24.185
Stewie could be anywhere.

12:39.133 --> 12:41.851
Sorry, I forgot my jacket.

12:46.891 --> 12:49.642
Okay, everybody, we're gonna
do some double-play drills.

12:49.643 --> 12:51.010
Oh, yeah, a little infield.

12:51.011 --> 12:52.478
Let's flash some leather, huh, guys?

12:52.479 --> 12:54.147
Who wants to play second?

12:54.148 --> 12:54.981
I will.

12:54.982 --> 12:56.983
Lois, why don't you take second?

12:57.944 --> 12:59.018
How could he not see that?

12:59.019 --> 13:01.254
I even held up my arm
with my other hand.

13:01.255 --> 13:02.722
That is the most noticeable way

13:02.723 --> 13:03.856
to raise your hand.

13:03.857 --> 13:04.957
Okay, Griffin, you go out there

13:04.958 --> 13:05.910
and be the base runner.

13:07.353 --> 13:09.328
All right, Peter, show 'em what you got.

13:09.329 --> 13:10.897
Okay, Lois, catch the ball,

13:10.898 --> 13:12.398
and if your foot comes off the bag,

13:12.399 --> 13:14.667
just tag Peter on any part of his body.

13:14.668 --> 13:16.269
How could I miss, right?

13:16.270 --> 13:18.004
It'll be like tagging a barn.

13:20.207 --> 13:22.675
Sorry, Peter, that's baseball.

13:22.676 --> 13:26.729
I'll show you baseball, you
sexually unsatisfied wife!

13:31.436 --> 13:34.003
Oh.

13:43.130 --> 13:46.332
Yeah! Now, that's a
big-league slide, huh, coach?

13:46.333 --> 13:47.934
Damn it!

13:47.935 --> 13:49.669
I think it's broken.

13:49.670 --> 13:51.404
Griffin, what are you, an idiot?

13:51.405 --> 13:53.239
Yeah, an idiot who's gonna show up

13:53.240 --> 13:55.341
<i>on SportsCenter tonight.</i>

13:55.342 --> 13:56.542
Coming up after the break,

13:56.543 --> 13:58.511
we'll have highlights of the
playoff game between...

13:58.512 --> 13:59.895
Streaking. Unrelated.

14:05.928 --> 14:07.311
Yep, her leg is fractured.

14:07.312 --> 14:08.679
We should get her to the hospital.

14:08.680 --> 14:11.215
My only medical training
is to say "Walk it off."

14:11.216 --> 14:12.917
- Can you walk it off?
- No!

14:12.918 --> 14:14.519
Oh, well, that's not good.

14:14.520 --> 14:17.255
Okay, I'm gonna go fake-use
the phone in the dugout.

14:17.256 --> 14:19.390
Peter, what the hell got into you?

14:19.391 --> 14:21.826
Nothing. I was just trying to
play hard, like Pete Rose.

14:21.827 --> 14:24.197
Look, I can even do the
Pete Rose haircut.

14:25.130 --> 14:28.099
I bet you a thousand bucks
I have a drinking problem.

14:28.100 --> 14:30.001
Guys, we got to get that leg set.

14:30.002 --> 14:31.702
I guess I should ride in the ambulance.

14:31.703 --> 14:33.437
You think I'll be back
in time for the game?

14:33.438 --> 14:35.373
What? You're not playing in the game.

14:35.374 --> 14:36.974
It's supposed to be a fun day out here,

14:36.975 --> 14:39.310
and you go nuts and
break your wife's leg.

14:39.311 --> 14:40.945
It's not my fault, I'm all hopped up

14:40.946 --> 14:43.091
on hard baseball card gum.

14:47.937 --> 14:51.355
Mmm, it's like eating a MasterCard.

14:51.356 --> 14:52.850
Let's get her out of here.

14:54.510 --> 14:56.060
And you, you're done.

14:56.061 --> 14:57.630
Clean out your locker!

14:58.230 --> 15:01.198
Kicked out? I'm totally screwed.

15:01.199 --> 15:02.733
Like those poor guys who had to come up

15:02.734 --> 15:05.002
with a new ad campaign for Subway.

15:05.003 --> 15:06.504
Hey, I'm Mike.

15:06.505 --> 15:09.073
I like sandwiches and people my own age.

15:09.074 --> 15:12.426
<i> Subway... please don't
think of pedophilia.</i>

15:19.068 --> 15:20.918
You know what I'm
getting sick of saying?

15:20.919 --> 15:23.955
"My husband did this to me,
but it's not what you think."

15:23.956 --> 15:26.424
Please forgive me, Lois. I'm so stupid.

15:26.425 --> 15:28.159
The reason I didn't bring my friends is

15:28.160 --> 15:30.261
'cause I didn't want 'em
hogging the spotlight.

15:30.262 --> 15:32.597
And then when I saw everyone
giving you all that attention,

15:32.598 --> 15:34.966
I-I guess I kind of lost it.

15:34.967 --> 15:36.801
You did a little.

15:36.802 --> 15:39.170
But of course I forgive you.

15:39.171 --> 15:42.006
I just don't understand
why you went so crazy.

15:42.007 --> 15:43.874
Well, ever since I was little,

15:43.875 --> 15:45.876
I was always the fat, uncoordinated kid

15:45.877 --> 15:47.511
that nobody wanted on their team.

15:47.512 --> 15:49.580
And I was excited that for one weekend,

15:49.581 --> 15:51.315
if I could just step on that field

15:51.316 --> 15:53.150
and get a hit at Fenway Park,

15:53.151 --> 15:55.286
I could erase all that
and feel like a champ

15:55.287 --> 15:56.921
for the first time in my life.

15:56.922 --> 16:00.524
But I'm not a champ, I'm a fat loser.

16:00.525 --> 16:02.242
No wonder nobody ever picked me.

16:04.880 --> 16:06.564
I picked you, Peter.

16:06.565 --> 16:10.201
And to me and our kids, you
will always be a winner.

16:10.202 --> 16:12.003
Thanks, Lois.

16:12.004 --> 16:13.738
And you know what? If that's true,

16:13.739 --> 16:15.473
I don't need to play in some stupid

16:15.474 --> 16:17.074
fantasy baseball game.

16:17.075 --> 16:18.209
Well, guess what.

16:18.210 --> 16:19.410
You're gonna play in that game,

16:19.411 --> 16:20.778
and you're gonna get that hit.

16:20.779 --> 16:22.847
And when you do, we're
all gonna be there

16:22.848 --> 16:23.981
to cheer you on.

16:23.982 --> 16:26.384
Really? Well, how's that gonna happen?

16:26.385 --> 16:28.486
Peter, these guys have
been sexually harassing me

16:28.487 --> 16:29.854
since the second I got here.

16:29.855 --> 16:31.922
Either you play, or every
one of these Red Sox

16:31.923 --> 16:34.692
are going to jail... Even Ted Williams.

16:34.693 --> 16:36.293
Mmm, new meat.

16:36.294 --> 16:38.829
I think we're gonna get along just fine.

16:38.830 --> 16:40.531
This is the number-one fear

16:40.532 --> 16:42.210
of only being a head.

16:46.322 --> 16:49.974
Brian, do you always listen to
the Sirius XM preview station?

16:49.975 --> 16:51.742
Yeah, I'm thinking about
pulling the trigger,

16:51.743 --> 16:53.210
but they make you sign,
like, a two-year...

16:53.211 --> 16:55.012
Guys, who cares about your dumb radio?!

16:55.013 --> 16:56.914
We can't find Stewie anywhere.

16:57.916 --> 17:01.385
Hello. Oh, hi, Mom.

17:01.386 --> 17:03.054
Hi, honey. How you doing?

17:03.055 --> 17:04.388
How's Stewie?

17:04.389 --> 17:06.657
Oh, he's great. Not lost or anything.

17:06.658 --> 17:08.626
How's fantasy camp going?

17:08.627 --> 17:10.828
Uh, your father broke
my leg out of jealousy,

17:10.829 --> 17:12.396
but that didn't ruin our honeymoon,

17:12.397 --> 17:13.731
and it's not gonna ruin this.

17:13.732 --> 17:16.167
So listen, I want all you guys

17:16.168 --> 17:18.002
to drive up to Boston this afternoon

17:18.003 --> 17:20.071
to see your father play in the big game.

17:20.072 --> 17:22.339
Uh, wow, we'd love to...

17:22.340 --> 17:24.909
Mom, but we promised Stewie

17:24.910 --> 17:28.579
we'd perform a puppet
show for him later today.

17:28.580 --> 17:31.549
Oh, you can perform it for
all of us up here in Boston.

17:31.550 --> 17:33.050
The game's in two hours.

17:33.051 --> 17:34.819
Drive safely.

17:34.820 --> 17:38.038
<i>Crap! Now we got to find Stewie
and write a puppet show.</i>

17:39.850 --> 17:42.193
We could repurpose my one-act farce.

17:42.194 --> 17:45.021
<i>Or we could write something fresh.</i>

17:45.022 --> 17:46.363
Look, just because it's
already been written

17:46.364 --> 17:47.898
doesn't mean it's not fresh.

17:47.899 --> 17:50.134
What did I just say? Shut up!

17:50.135 --> 17:53.003
<i>We're in trouble. I'm in trouble.</i>

17:53.004 --> 17:55.005
Hey, what's this, a dickweed convention?

17:55.006 --> 17:56.040
Stewie!

17:56.041 --> 17:57.374
Oh, thank God you're home!

17:57.375 --> 17:58.909
Where the hell have you been?

17:58.910 --> 18:01.345
<i>As far away from her as possible.</i>

18:01.346 --> 18:02.780
I forgot her name, honestly.

18:02.781 --> 18:05.791
- Who, Meg?
- Yes, yes, Meg. She's scary and mean,

18:05.793 --> 18:08.018
and I don't ever want her
to be in charge of me.

18:08.019 --> 18:10.154
Are you afraid of me, little guy?

18:10.155 --> 18:14.194
Oh, Stewie, I'm really sorry
I left you in that time-out.

18:14.196 --> 18:17.628
I love you very much, and
I'm so happy you're home.

18:17.629 --> 18:19.630
You're my little brother.

18:19.631 --> 18:21.000
Can you forgive me?

18:21.626 --> 18:24.468
Well... all right.

18:29.708 --> 18:31.208
Can I have your baby?

18:31.209 --> 18:32.381
Don't let her in!

18:39.976 --> 18:41.351
We're all proud of you, Peter.

18:41.353 --> 18:42.753
N-Now, don't be nervous.

18:42.754 --> 18:44.688
I ain't nervous, Lois...
I'm just sweating

18:44.689 --> 18:47.424
'cause I was too embarrassed to
get nude in the locker room,

18:47.425 --> 18:49.527
so I'm wearing all this
over long pajamas.

18:49.528 --> 18:51.929
Ladies and gentlemen, now batting

18:51.930 --> 18:56.100
for the Boston Red Sox, Peter Griffin!

19:13.118 --> 19:15.869
Fair ball! Run, Peter! Run it out!

19:20.492 --> 19:21.725
Peter's Brain.

19:21.726 --> 19:23.594
Yeah, uh, this is the Muscle Department.

19:23.595 --> 19:25.262
What the hell is he doing?

19:25.263 --> 19:27.631
Uh, apparently, he's trying to sprint.

19:27.632 --> 19:29.900
Sprint? He got winded
walking to the plate.

19:29.901 --> 19:32.770
And he's been out in the
blazing sun for two days.

19:32.771 --> 19:34.505
Has he had any water?

19:34.506 --> 19:37.541
No. He told his wife there's
juices in the hot dogs.

19:37.542 --> 19:39.443
Well, I'm sorry, I got no choice

19:39.444 --> 19:41.795
but to call for a
complete muscle failure.

19:47.819 --> 19:49.119
Look! Dad's planking,

19:49.120 --> 19:50.821
from, like, eight years ago!

19:50.822 --> 19:52.823
Is there a Neiman Marcus in Boston?

19:52.824 --> 19:55.776
Peter! Get up! Get up and run!

19:57.479 --> 19:58.929
- Run, Peter!
- Come on, Dad!

19:58.930 --> 20:01.949
- We love you!
- Copley Place. How far is that?

20:12.194 --> 20:16.005
<i>I ran like a champion that
day, pushing through the pain</i>

20:16.006 --> 20:18.550
<i>of two torn hamstrings
and a ruptured groin,</i>

20:18.551 --> 20:20.510
<i>to leg out the hit at Fenway Park</i>

20:20.511 --> 20:22.513
<i>I had always dreamed of.</i>

20:23.421 --> 20:26.590
<i>But nobody noticed, 'cause the
account manager from B of A</i>

20:26.591 --> 20:29.026
<i>who was playing third base
had a massive coronary</i>

20:29.027 --> 20:31.647
<i>trying to field my crappy little nubber.</i>

20:32.214 --> 20:35.599
<i>The hit was amazing, but
what made it even better</i>

20:35.600 --> 20:38.502
<i>was that my family was there
to share the moment with me.</i>

20:38.503 --> 20:41.005
<i>And on the car ride home,
they put on a puppet show</i>

20:41.006 --> 20:44.008
<i>that made me laugh so hard
I crashed into a tollbooth</i>

20:44.009 --> 20:46.043
<i>on the Mass Pike, totaling the car</i>

20:46.044 --> 20:48.045
<i>and breaking Lois's other leg.</i>

20:48.046 --> 20:49.847
<i>The casts kind of smell,</i>

20:49.848 --> 20:52.549
<i>so I won't let her sleep in
the bedroom till they're off.</i>

20:52.550 --> 20:54.351
<i>But that's baseball.</i>

20:54.358 --> 20:57.072
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru